# Limited-length strings (ed.3 6.4.4.1 table 10 / ed.2 2.3.1 table 10):
# `STRING[n]` holds up to n characters; a value of at most n characters is
# stored whole; the declared initial value applies; a named type may be a
# STRING[n]. Values here are all within the declared lengths (the longer
# case is undefined/string_truncate).
# No inputs; two cycles.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs:
outputs: s3 s4 s5 n3 n4 n5 cat
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.4.4.1 table 10 (STRING[n]), 6.4.4.4 (initial values)
---
0 => s3='xyz' s4='init' s5='abcde' n3=3 n4=4 n5=5 cat='xyzinit'
1 => s3='xyz' s4='init' s5='abcde' n3=3 n4=4 n5=5 cat='xyzinit'
